  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "On September 15, 2026, Blanche described AI as extraordinarily beneficial to society and characterized the timing of public fears about it as politically motivated. In the November 5, 2026 statements attributed to him as attorney general, Blanche described a Justice Department super-intelligence task force and pledged continued prosecution of unlawful uses targeting Americans, infrastructure, or national security. In undated excerpts, Blanche opposed additional AI regulation at that time and described the Justice Department's role as prosecution rather than regulation.",
   "sids": [
